From 9102be92025becdefedb71fa06ec60be16176ef3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EvilPatrick06 <187923600+EvilPatrick06@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:37:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] desktop: resolve a switch target's descriptor in the dial,
 not inside the commit

A source switch dialed the target's socket in phase one, then looked up its
connection descriptor inside the commit, under the commit's local 20 s
budget, after the previous backend's bindings were already severed. The
commit only lands once that descriptor is published (targetIsActive), and
the lookup can cross into a remote bring-up: a retained socket can still be
open while main's pooled backend for the route is being rebuilt (its ssh
tunnel dropped when the remote dashboard restarted). Then the lookup waits
for a whole remote boot, the commit times out, and the switch fails with
"did not become active" while the target is still coming up. Measured: the
activation moved the route at 14:19:09.182, no descriptor was published,
the switch gave up at 14:19:29.350, and the remote dashboards bound at
14:19:35 and 14:19:36.

openGatewayAgent now resolves the descriptor together with the socket, on
the caller's dial budget, and returns it; a failed lookup fails the dial
before anything is touched. selectConnection hands it to ensureGatewayAgent,
which publishes it without a lookup of its own. Callers that pass no
descriptor (the SDK and session doors) look it up as before.
